  "fields": {
    "summary": "[ci-heal] run-name contract: group token must lead the run-name",
    "description": "**Run-name contract** (self-heal observability): for every parameterized factory-owned workflow, the `run-name` FIRST token must be the stable group key - it must contain the dispatch parameter (`inputs.*` / issue number) and must NOT contain run-varying values (`run_id`, `run_number`, timestamps, SHAs).

**Non-conforming:** Geo Probe

**Fix:** restructure the `run-name` so the group token leads, e.g. `run-name: gh- - dev` for an issue-parameterized leg. Plain (non-parameterized) workflows may use the workflow name as the token.

**Why:** the self-heal legs-health detector groups runs by the first run-name token; without a leading group token a chronically failing parameter is invisible (interleaved greens reset raw streaks). The fix must ONLY adjust `run-name` - no behavioral changes. Use `Closes #<this issue>`.

